FOMO host tests

Run from the project root after notebook export:
  .venv/bin/python -m unittest discover -s test -p 'test_*.py' -v

Requires a host C++ compiler and requirements-local.txt. Tests compile fomo_host.cpp
in a temporary directory, then compare the actual firmware decoder/preprocessor
with the notebook's Python implementation. Also verifies exported model bytes,
int8 tensor contracts, supported operators, and the static inference fixture.

Compile the camera and static firmware environments with PlatformIO. Use the
static image on hardware to validate TFLite Micro against static-expected.json.
